- op: discuss  # 81f8
  at: '2026-07-16T07:56:36Z'  # 81f8
  by: agent  # 81f8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 81f8
  clock: 8  # 81f8
  nonce: 81f8  # 81f8
  message: "REOPENED + reprioritized P4->P2 (per this item 2026-07-16 reproduction note). BUILD-WRAPPER FACET FIXED (dev 471bb5a779): mvnw/gradlew are demoted below the ranking floor in detect_entrypoints (x0.1 + connectivity-boost skip, keyed on EntrypointKind.SHELL_SCRIPT + a build-wrapper basename allowlist {mvnw,mvnw.cmd,gradlew,gradlew.bat}), so they no longer seed forward slices. BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: live spring-petclinic survey — mvnw/gradlew were the top-2 of 44 entrypoints at rank_score 0.98 (above the real controllers at ~0.54); after the fix both are filtered out (44->42) and slice --entry auto no longer seeds from them. 3 unit tests + entrypoints.py 100% cov.\n\nREMAINING FACETS (item stays open as the seed-quality umbrella):\n1. is_utility_file over-matches samples/example/demo in SOURCE paths. On spring-petclinic (org.springframework.samples.petclinic) the real controllers get the x0.5 utility penalty (~0.54) AND are excluded from langs_with_semantic, so entity library_exports (Owner/Pet at 0.90) are NOT demoted and now win the seed after the mvnw fix. Demo-repo-specific: a real Spring app path -> is_utility_file False -> controllers win. Debatable (a sample repo IS demo code) but degrades intra-sample ranking.\n2. pretix seeds slice+rslice from vendored JS (pdf.worker.js/d3/vue.js) despite the tier-3 x0.3 penalty (0.80x0.3=0.24 > 0.10 floor). Vendored code may warrant a harder demotion or should not be a library_export entrypoint. Also folds in the original fix-sketch rslice-tier-1-constraint facet.\n3. express #1 symbol = test-file callback createApp (in=202) is COMPACT/centrality ranking (ranking.py symbol centrality), a DIFFERENT subsystem from entrypoint seed selection — belongs with WI-zulij, not this entrypoint fix."  # 81f8
