- op: discuss  # ea6f
  at: '2026-07-29T04:15:48Z'  # ea6f
  by: agent  # ea6f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ea6f
  clock: 12  # ea6f
  nonce: ea6f  # ea6f
  message: "CLOSED done (2026-07-29, PR #62, dev 211ec3ba91). The two remaining\nseed-selection facets are fixed at the ranking chokepoint; the third is split\nout; the fourth was never this item's.\n\nPREMISE CORRECTION -- the 2026-07-21 \"bakeoff-gated ranking TUNING, magnitude is\na judgment call\" framing was WRONG on mechanism, and that is why this sat parked.\nBoth real causes are STRUCTURAL and testable without a bakeoff:\n\n(1) CARVE-OUT SCOPE, not magnitude. The library_export x0.1 demotion is gated on\n    `lang in langs_with_semantic` -- a carve-out written to protect FIRST-PARTY\n    API surface (the ArkLib case: 6 Python helper scripts must not suppress 163\n    Lean exports). Vendored third-party code is never the analyzed repo's API\n    surface in ANY language, so the carve-out no longer extends to tier>=3.\n    Scoped by supply-chain TIER, so the existing axis does the work instead of a\n    second hand-curated vendor-path allowlist.\n\n(2) THE DEMOTION ALONE DID NOT WORK -- the half the filed arithmetic\n    (\"0.80x0.3=0.24 > the 0.10 floor\") missed. The connectivity boost is\n    ADDITIVE: x0.1 -> 0.0225 plus an in-degree boost of up to +0.35 climbs\n    straight back over the floor. Caught ONLY by the real-repo A/B; the unit\n    test for (1) passed while the live ranking was unmoved. The codebase had\n    already learned this twice -- infra_export_ids (77 gemini-cli telemetry\n    exports surviving at ~0.14 purely on the boost) and build_wrapper_ids\n    (mvnw/gradlew, this item's own earlier fix) -- so all three now share one\n    `boost_suppressed_ids` set and one skip check rather than a third parallel\n    set the next category would have to rediscover.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (production path, real repo, A/B on identical nodes+edges --\nonly the ranking function differs). `hypergumbo survey .` on\n~/ALL_REPOS/curriculum_repos/zellij (has zellij-utils/src/vendored/termwiz,\ntier-3 via the INV-kokik `vendored/` rule), then detect_entrypoints re-run\nagainst the same survey with the fix stashed in/out:\n  BEFORE: 2 tier>=3 entrypoints survive -- InputParser::parse rank=0.6009,\n          InputParser::new rank=0.5740\n  AFTER:  0 tier>=3 entrypoints survive; the top-ranked first-party seeds\n          (src/main.rs:main, the web_client http_handlers) are unchanged.\nHarness was itself controlled: confirmed `git stash` actually removed\n`is_vendored` from the module and that the module resolved to the repo path,\nbecause an identical before/after is exactly what a broken A/B produces.\nUnit tests: a vendored export with a realistic in-degree of 13 (zellij's actual\nfigure) stays filtered, plus an ArkLib guard asserting a tier-1 export in a\nlanguage with no semantic entrypoints keeps its full 0.75 -- non-vacuous, it\nfails if the carve-out is dropped wholesale instead of narrowed.\n2003 passed / 1 skipped, 100% coverage on changed files.\n\nFACET DISPOSITION (all four, explicitly):\n - vendored-JS/Rust seeds: FIXED (above).\n - reverse-slice tier-seed constraint: COVERED, and the filed fix DECLINED as\n   written. `slice --entry auto` and `--reverse` resolve seeds through the SAME\n   detect_entrypoints call (cli.py), so the vendored fix reaches both. A blanket\n   \"constrain reverse-slice seeds to tier 1\" would be WRONG: tier 2 is\n   internal_dep -- genuinely first-party monorepo code and a legitimate seed --\n   and `--max-tier` already exists as the explicit user knob.\n - is_utility_file over-match on samples/example/demo: SPLIT OUT to\n   WI-dojij-tamit-mupag-nopun-fogiz-dofin-takav-zijog (P3, todo_soft). Distinct\n   mechanism (path-predicate precision) with a real design fork; this item's own\n   note flagged it debatable.\n - express test-file callback createApp (in=202): NOT this item -- compact /\n   centrality ranking, belongs to WI-zulij. Recorded here so it is not lost.\n\nBuild-wrapper facet remains fixed (471bb5a779)."  # ea6f
